  "description": "TANJIF crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P 1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C55 H111 Cr3 N3 O27 Y3,3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Cr1 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr2 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr3 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Y1 (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Y2 (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Y3 (Y) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.310-3.989 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.23-114.18°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C55H117Cr3Y3N3O30. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
